12. Loop Engineering Logic

The loop:


Evaluate current policy.
Collect failed cases.
Group failures by pattern.
Agent explains the pattern.
Revision engine applies bounded changes.
Retest.
Stop when thresholds pass or max iterations reached.


Bounded policy updates:

ConditionActionSafe young businesses are rejectedLower minBusinessAgeMonths by 6 monthsRisky borrowers are approvedIncrease minCreditScore by 10, or reduce maxDebtToIncomeRatio by 0.03Collateral-backed borrowers are rejectedAdd manual review rule for collateralRatio >= 0.6Too many manual reviewsTighten clear approval/rejection thresholdsDefault risk is too highTighten debt ratio and cash flow requirements

13. Agent Layer

Use agents for critique and explanation, not final scoring.

Agent responsibilities:


Analyze failed cases
Explain why the policy failed
Suggest safe policy changes
Generate final report


Important rule: The evaluator is deterministic. The agent recommends and explains.

Fallback: If no LLM API is ready, use templated agent explanations.

